        "original_id": "8b1a8f3f-0eaf-5dc1-b0c8-ea8e142c1a99",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Happiest Millionaire, Mars Needs Moms, A Christmas Carol\n- Songs: Fortuosity\n- People: Fred MacMurray, Anthony J. Drexel Biddle, Berkeley Breathed\n- Companies: The Walt Disney Company, ImageMovers, The Walt Disney Studios\n- Projects: ImageMovers Digital\n\nFacts:\n- The Happiest Millionaire is a 1967 musical film starring Fred MacMurray.\n- The Happiest Millionaire is based on the true story of Philadelphia millionaire Anthony J. Drexel Biddle.\n- \"Fortuosity\" is the first song in the 1967 motion picture The Happiest Millionaire.\n- From 2007 to 2010, The Walt Disney Company and ImageMovers operated the joint animation facility ImageMovers Digital.\n- ImageMovers Digital produced the performance-captured animated films A Christmas Carol and Mars Needs Moms for The Walt Disney Studios.\n- Mars Needs Moms is a 2011 American computer-animated film based on the Berkeley Breathed book of the same title.",
